# Vulnerabilities accepted, not fixed — reviewed 2026-08-04.
#
# 2026-09-11: frontend/Dockerfile now rebuilds caddy from source on a
# current Go toolchain, and the frontend image scans clean with NO ignore
# file at all. The five entries below no longer protect the image they
# were written for. They are left in place only because this file is
# root-level and applies to every image in the build matrix (api, worker,
# mcp_server, cli), whose scans were cancelled in CI before this change
# and have not been re-checked without it. Delete them once they are.
#
# All five below are compiled into the `caddy` binary itself (Go stdlib,
# golang.org/x/text, and grpc-go), inside the official caddy:2-alpine
# Docker image (frontend/Dockerfile). They are not Alpine apk packages, so
# `apk upgrade` can't touch them — fixing them requires the Caddy
# maintainers to rebuild their published image against patched Go module
# versions. Confirmed against Docker Hub on 2026-08-04 that caddy:2-alpine
# already points at their newest build (2.11.3, pushed 18 days prior) —
# there is currently no newer upstream image that fixes these.
#
# Re-check this file next time frontend/Dockerfile's base image is
# touched, or periodically: if caddy:2-alpine has been rebuilt since
# 2026-08-04, remove the corresponding line(s) below and let Trivy catch
# anything still unfixed for real.

CVE-2026-56852       # golang.org/x/text — norm.Iter infinite loop
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf   # google.golang.org/grpc — xDS RBAC / HTTP/2 issues
CVE-2026-27145        # Go stdlib crypto/x509 — DoS via excessive DNS name processing
CVE-2026-39822        # Go stdlib os.Root — symlink-following directory traversal
CVE-2026-42504        # Go stdlib mime — DoS via malicious MIME header
